IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`
IMPORT `ssc3-a-s43-s44`
IMPORT `ssc3-e-s51-s55`

-- Tests for ssc3-e-s51-s55.l4 (ss 51, 51ZA, 51A, 52, 55).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it; none is copied from the encoding's output.
-- The fixtures' dates are chosen for the comparisons under test; a fixture is not a claim about when anyone really attains pensionable age (that is the keel's fact, ssc-core.l4).

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `their sex` IS A Sex
      born IS A DATE
      attained IS A DATE
GIVETH A Person
`a person` MEANS
    Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS born
        `sex` IS `their sex`
        `marital status` IS `married`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS attained

`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005` MEANS `a person` Man (Date 1 1 1940) (Date 1 1 2005)
`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005` MEANS `a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 1 1 2005)
`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004` MEANS `a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1944) (Date 1 1 2004)
`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004` MEANS `a person` Man (Date 1 1 1939) (Date 1 1 2004)

§ `Section 51: Category B retirement pension for widows, widowers and surviving civil partners who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010`

-- (3): paragraph 5 where the spouse attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010; paragraph 5A on or after it.
#ASSERT `s 51(3) the relevant contribution condition` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 5 4 2010)) EQUALS `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
#ASSERT `s 51(3) the relevant contribution condition` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) EQUALS `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`
-- (5): the same for the deceased civil partner.
#ASSERT `s 51(5) the relevant contribution condition` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 5 4 2010)) EQUALS `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
#ASSERT `s 51(5) the relevant contribution condition` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) EQUALS `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`
-- (2): a woman whose husband has died; a man whose wife died before 6 April 1979; no one else.
#ASSERT `s 51(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008)
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008)))
#ASSERT `s 51(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 5 4 1979)
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 6 4 1979)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51(2) subsection (1) does not confer a right on the person` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 5 4 1979)))
-- 51ZA(4): a woman whose dead spouse was, at death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and whose marriage subsisted before it.
#ASSERT `s 51ZA(4) section 51(1) does not confer a right on the woman` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(4) section 51(1) does not confer a right on the woman` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(4) section 51(1) does not confer a right on the woman` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(4) section 51(1) does not confer a right on the woman` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE TRUE))
-- (1): a man whose wife died on 1 January 2008 while married; both had attained pensionable age; the pensioner before 6 April 2010; the wife (attained 1 January 2004) needs paragraph 5.
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(a): "over pensionable age" is "has attained": the day of attaining counts (section 173(a)); the day before does not.
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2005) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 31 12 2004) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2004) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(b): the pensioner attained pensionable age on 6 April 2010: too late.
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 5 4 2010)) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(c): a spouse who attained pensionable age on 6 April 2010 needs paragraph 5A, not paragraph 5.
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): a woman whose husband has died is shut out; a man whose wife died before 6 April 1979 is shut out.
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970)) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970)) (Date 5 4 1979) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970)) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970)) (Date 6 4 1979) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 51ZA(4) is a bar on (1): a woman whose dead spouse was, at death, a woman by gender recognition.
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4): a civil partner; the deceased civil partner (attained 1 January 2004) needs paragraph 5.
#ASSERT `s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2008) FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A deceased civil partner who attained pensionable age on 6 April 2010 needs paragraph 5A; the pensioner attained it on 1 January 2009.
#ASSERT `s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1944) (Date 1 1 2009)) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 51(4) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1944) (Date 1 1 2009)) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1945) (Date 6 4 2010)) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): references to the pensioner are taken as references to the spouse or deceased civil partner.
#ASSERT `s 51(6) the person to whom a reference to the pensioner is taken to refer` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) TRUE EQUALS JUST (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`)
#ASSERT `s 51(6) the person to whom a reference to the pensioner is taken to refer` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7): the additional pension is halved for a man whose wife dies after 5 October 2002, for a surviving party to a marriage of a same sex couple, and for a surviving civil partner.
#ASSERT `s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 6 10 2002) FALSE (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 5 10 2002) FALSE (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 6 10 2002) FALSE (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 1999) FALSE (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 1999) FALSE (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 1 1 1999) TRUE (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 51(7) the amount of additional pension after any halving in pounds` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2004`) (Date 6 10 2002) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): the rate is the basic pension plus the additional pension after halving.
#ASSERT `s 51(6) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` (JUST 184.9) (JUST 20) EQUALS JUST 204.9
#ASSERT `s 51(6) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` NOTHING (JUST 20) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 51(6) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds` (JUST 184.9) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8): no account of earnings factors for 2016-17 or later.
#ASSERT `s 51(8) the earnings factor of the spouse or deceased civil partner for the tax year is taken into account` (`Tax year` OF 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 51(8) the earnings factor of the spouse or deceased civil partner for the tax year is taken into account` (`Tax year` OF 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9): entitlement begins on the day the conditions are satisfied and continues throughout life.
#ASSERT `s 51(9) the entitlement to a Category B retirement pension under section 51 is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 31 12 2019) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 51(9) the entitlement to a Category B retirement pension under section 51 is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 51(9) the entitlement to a Category B retirement pension under section 51 is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 51(9) the entitlement to a Category B retirement pension under section 51 is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 2 1 2025) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (11) and (12): the additional pension rises by the orders' percentage when the spouse or civil partner attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016 and died after attaining it. 20 x (1 + 10/100) = 22.
#ASSERT `s 51(12) the weekly rate of the additional pension after the increase in pounds` TRUE TRUE 20 (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `s 51(12) the weekly rate of the additional pension after the increase in pounds` TRUE TRUE 20 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 51(12) the weekly rate of the additional pension after the increase in pounds` FALSE TRUE 20 (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 51(12) the weekly rate of the additional pension after the increase in pounds` TRUE FALSE 20 (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST 20

§ `Section 51ZA: special provision for married person whose spouse changed gender`

-- (1): section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent a woman whose spouse is a woman by gender recognition and whose marriage subsisted before the certificate.
#ASSERT `s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE TRUE))
-- (2): section 48AA(2)(b), for the former spouse at the time the marriage was dissolved.
#ASSERT `s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE FALSE))
-- (3): section 48B(1ZA)(b), for the dead spouse at the time of death; the same case also changes the reading of section 48B(1ZB)(a)(ii).
#ASSERT `s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` (`a man who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2005`) TRUE TRUE))

§ `Section 51A: special provision for married people`

-- (1): this section has effect where the person would be entitled to both pensions apart from section 43(1).
#ASSERT `s 51A(1) this section has effect` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51A(1) this section has effect` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51A(1) this section has effect` FALSE TRUE))
-- (3): not where both parties attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979.
#ASSERT `s 51A(3) this section does not apply` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 5 4 1979)) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51A(3) this section does not apply` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 6 4 1979)) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970))))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 51A(3) this section does not apply` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970)) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 6 4 1979))))
-- (2): the shortfall below the Schedule 4 figure (150) of a basic pension of 100 is 50; the increase is the lesser of that and the Category B rate.
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 (JUST 150) 30 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 (JUST 150) 60 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 (JUST 150) 50 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 150 (JUST 150) 30 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 160 (JUST 150) 30 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 (JUST 150) 30 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 (JUST 150) 30 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (JUST 150) 30 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1990)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 NOTHING 30 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Both parties attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979: the section does not apply, whatever else is unknown.
#ASSERT `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1970)) (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 1 1 1975)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 NOTHING 30 EQUALS JUST 0

§ `Section 52: special provision for surviving spouses`

-- (1): this section has effect where the person would be entitled to both pensions apart from section 43(1).
#ASSERT `s 52(1) this section has effect` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 52(1) this section has effect` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 52(1) this section has effect` FALSE TRUE))
-- (4): not where the death was before 6 April 1979 and the surviving spouse had attained pensionable age before that date.
#ASSERT `s 52(4) this section does not apply` (Date 5 4 1979) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 5 4 1979))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 52(4) this section does not apply` (Date 6 4 1979) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 5 4 1979))))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 52(4) this section does not apply` (Date 5 4 1979) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 6 4 1979))))
-- (2): the full amount is 184.90; a basic pension of 100 falls short by 84.90; the increase is the lesser of that and the Category B basic pension.
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 30 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 100 EQUALS JUST 84.9
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 184.9 100 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 190 100 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 100 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 100 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 5 4 1979) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 5 4 1979)) TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 100 EQUALS JUST 0
-- (3A): the additional pension for (3) leaves out the units. 15 - 5 = 10.
#ASSERT `s 52(3A) the additional pension for subsection (3) in pounds` 15 5 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 52(3A) the additional pension for subsection (3) in pounds` 15 0 EQUALS 15
-- (3): an additional pension of 10 falls short of the maximum 25 by 15; the increase is the lesser of that and the Category B additional pension.
#ASSERT `s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE 10 (JUST 25) 8 EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE 10 (JUST 25) 20 EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE 25 (JUST 25) 20 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE 30 (JUST 25) 20 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE 10 NOTHING 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) FALSE TRUE 10 (JUST 25) 20 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 52(3) the increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 5 4 1979) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 5 4 1979)) TRUE TRUE 10 NOTHING 20 EQUALS JUST 0
-- (3B): an amount attributable to units in the Category B pension raises the Category A additional pension by that amount.
#ASSERT `s 52(3B) the further increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE TRUE 4 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 52(3B) the further increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 1 1 1990) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1925) (Date 1 1 1985)) TRUE FALSE 4 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 52(3B) the further increase of the additional pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds` (Date 5 4 1979) (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1905) (Date 5 4 1979)) TRUE TRUE 4 EQUALS 0

§ `Section 55: pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to retirement pension is deferred`

-- (3): deferred if and so long as (a) the person does not become entitled by reason only of not satisfying the conditions of section 1 of the Administration Act (the claim), or (b) an election under section 54(1) treats the person as not having become entitled.
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3), under the name the other seam uses.
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the pension is deferred` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the pension is deferred` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55(3) the pension is deferred` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): Schedule 5 has effect where entitlement is deferred.
#ASSERT `s 55(1) Schedule 5 has effect` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55(1) Schedule 5 has effect` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55(1) Schedule 5 has effect` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
